//@variable Forecast display description.
export const string TT_FORECAST = "■ Forecast (show predicted level at bar close)"
 + "\n\nThe following requires 'Forecast' selected:"
 + "\n■ ⁒ (Bar Elapsed Time Percent)"
 + "\n■ x (Multiplier, level relative to MA)"
 + "\n■ Level (Area in between levels)"
 + "\n■ Color (Forecast level sets label's color)"
 + "\n■ Instance (🔎Forecast and/or ✅Current)"
 + "\n(Current also referred to as known or now)"
 + "\n\n•Volume Forecast: assumes volume rate persists and uses current volume and bar time till close."
 + "\n•Spread Forecast: dynamically applies a multiplier (set later in settings), indicating that spread increases less when price is near the midpoint and more near low or high. In addition to these assumptions, the price change for spread to increase is also accounted for."
 + "\n•Moving Average: sourced from the bar's forecasted level instead current level. Ensures forecasting correct state (low,normal,high,ultra)."

